                "help": "Mark this run **interactive** (human-driven). The supervisor then never auto-terminalizes or auto-tears-down from a dead pid or a worker exit — it waits for an explicit `run merge` (→ teardown) or `run cancel`; the human owns the whole lifecycle (design.md §6). Opt-in; omit it (the default) for an autonomous fire-and-forget worker. This is the explicit how-run state that replaced the removed `code` kind — orthogonal to `--kind`, so any topology can be interactive",
